{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:j2s3-pilot-stress-test",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Fix bounded \\(h_f,h_c\\geq0\\) and \\(d\\geq0\\).  Form a \\(J=2\\), \\(S=3\\) array by retaining the pre laws, weights, donor post laws, and no-intervention span of \\(\\mathrm{def:j2s2\\mbox{-}instance}\\), while replacing the treated observed post law by masses \\(1/2\\), \\(d/\\sqrt{m_\\ell}\\), and \\(1/2-d/\\sqrt{m_\\ell}\\) at \\(0\\), \\(1/2\\), and \\(1\\), respectively, for all sufficiently large \\(\\ell\\).  This array belongs to \\(\\mathcal M\\).  If \\(N_\\ell\\) is the pilot count at the middle atom, then \\(\\sqrt{m_\\ell}N_\\ell/\\lceil m_\\ell^{3/4}\\rceil\\to d\\) in probability.  The certified procedure retains the bounded face offset \\(h_f\\) and bounded cross-cell translation \\(h_c\\) in its nuisance supremum, its DKW fallback probability tends to zero, and its normalized squared radius converges conditionally to \\(c^*(\\eta,\\alpha)\\).  This is a bounded-offset stress test and does not imply convergence on the slowly diverging diagonal arrays of \\(\\mathrm{lem:pilot\\mbox{-}resolution\\mbox{-}obstruction}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(J\\)",
      "\\(S\\)",
      "\\(h_f\\)",
      "\\(h_c\\)",
      "\\(m_\\ell\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M\\)",
      "\\(c^*(\\eta,\\alpha)\\)",
      "\\(\\eta\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:j2s2-instance",
      "thm:pilot-resolvable-certified-calibration",
      "lem:pilot-resolution-obstruction",
      "ass:stable-quantile-span"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "The pre-period laws and weights are those of \\(\\mathrm{def:j2s2\\mbox{-}instance}\\), so the smooth-density bounds, exact pre span, and the Gram lower bound \\(0<\\lambda\\leq1/375\\) remain valid.  The donor post laws are unchanged.  The modified treated law has three ordered atoms in \\([0,2]\\), and its masses are nonnegative for all sufficiently large \\(\\ell\\) because \\(d\\) is fixed and \\(m_\\ell\\to\\infty\\).  Defining the unobserved no-intervention law by the same donor quantile span preserves \\(\\mathrm{ass:stable\\mbox{-}quantile\\mbox{-}span}\\).  Cell sampling remains independent.  Hence every defining condition of \\(\\mathcal M\\) holds with \\(S=3\\).\n\nThe pilot middle-atom count is binomial with size\n\\(r_{m,\\ell}=\\lceil m_\\ell^{3/4}\\rceil\\) and success probability \\(d/\\sqrt{m_\\ell}\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n \\mathbb E\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{m_\\ell}N_\\ell}{r_{m,\\ell}}\\right)=d,\n \\qquad\n \\operatorname{Var}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{m_\\ell}N_\\ell}{r_{m,\\ell}}\\right)\n =\\frac{d\\sqrt{m_\\ell}}{r_{m,\\ell}}\n   \\left(1-\\frac d{\\sqrt{m_\\ell}}\\right)\\\\longrightarrow0.\n\\]\nThus Chebyshev's inequality proves learning of the internal offset.  Because \\(h_f\\) and \\(h_c\\) are bounded, they satisfy the bounded alternatives in\n\\(\\mathrm{thm:pilot\\mbox{-}resolvable\\mbox{-}certified\\mbox{-}calibration}\\): the procedure does not estimate them, but retains their full compatible sets in \\(\\Gamma_\\eta\\).  The theorem then gives vanishing fallback and conditional convergence to \\(c^*(\\eta,\\alpha)\\).  The obstruction lemma applies to offsets diverging more slowly than the pilot root-scale error, so this bounded experiment supplies no evidence for the excluded all-strata assertion.",
    "justification": "The strengthened early-kill instance verifies learnability of a root-\\(m_\\ell\\) within-cell mass while bounded face and cross-cell offsets remain nuisance.",
    "gap": "It is deliberately a bounded-offset stress test and does not address the slowly diverging diagonal obstruction.",
    "consumer": "It gives a concrete two-donor, three-atom certification test before any mosquito-abundance implementation.",
